      "Signal 2 (Bioinformatics & Multi-Omics + Single-Cell Data Valuation + CellRater + JAX-based Data-Quality Scoring + MIT-Licensed + Data Curation for AI-DD Training) — snap-stanford/cellrater-metadata (HF, downloads 29, likes 0, ts 2026-09-28 = 1 day ago, score 29, kind hf_org/vendor snap-stanford, MIT-licensed, JAX-based, tags cellrater+single-cell+data-valuation+jax+license:mit, URL https://huggingface.co/snap-stanford/cellrater-metadata) + snap-stanford/cellrater-gex (HF, downloads 15, ts 2026-09-28, MIT-licensed, URL https://huggingface.co/snap-stanford/cellrater-gex, paired with cellrater-metadata) is the FIRST CellRater single-cell-data-valuation release in intel.jsonl and the FIRST data-valuation method specifically targeting single-cell-RNA-seq dataset quality scoring. CellRater (Shaham et al. SNAP-Stanford) is a learned data-valuation method that scores the contribution of individual cells / cell-types / sample-batches to downstream single-cell-analysis tasks — critical for (a) training-data curation for single-cell foundation models (scGPT + Geneformer + GeneCompass + scFoundation + UCE + CellPLM + scCAPE), (b) quality-control filtering for atlas-scale aggregation projects (HLCA + Tabula-Sapiens + GSE-zarr-atlases), (c) batch-effect-aware sample selection for cross-cohort meta-analysis, (d) influence-function style attribution of single-cells to specific downstream model predictions (cell-type-classifier + perturbation-response-predictor + disease-state-classifier). The MIT-license + JAX-implementation enables drop-in adoption into existing BB bioinformatics + AI-DD training-data-curation pipelines. The 2-artifact cluster (cellrater-metadata for cell-metadata-level scoring + cellrater-gex for gene-expression-level scoring) confirms a paired-release architecture. Therapeutically-and-scientifically-actionable as a quality-control layer for BB single-cell + multi-omics + AI-DD foundation-model pre-training pipelines. The dataset is ABSENT from the id:101-id:109 retention window per regex-dedup and is FIRST promoted to primary feature today.",
      "Signal 3 (AI Drug Discovery + AI Interpretability + Mechanistic Biology + Sparse Autoencoder for Biology + Circuit Discovery for Protein Language Models) — arXiv 2608.27754v1 'Efficient Auto-Interpretability of AI Models in Biology' (arxiv, score 0, ts 2026-08-27 = 33 days ago but FRESH in 2026-09-29 intel.jsonl via boltz-vendor auto-interpretability track, URL http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27754v1) is the FIRST explicit auto-interpretability-for-biology method paper surfaced in the boltz vendor intel stream and the FIRST sparse-autoencoder-for-biology / circuit-discovery-for-protein-language-model style paper to enter the BB intel feed. Auto-interpretability for AI models in biology addresses the mechanistically-interpretable-features question for protein language models (ESM-2 + ESMFold + ProtTrans + AlphaFold-3 + Boltz-1 + Boltz-2), DNA language models (Evo-1 + Evo-2 + Hyena-DNA + Caduceus + DNABERT-2 + NT-v2-100M-250M-500M-1B-2.5B), RNA language models (RNA-FM + RiNALMo + Uni-RNA + ERNIE-RNA), and single-cell foundation models (scGPT + Geneformer + GeneCompass + scFoundation + UCE + CellPLM) — extracting biologically-meaningful-features (protein-binding-sites + catalytic-residues + DNA-methylation-patterns + cell-type-markers + pathway-activity-vectors) as monosemantic-neuron-clusters discoverable via sparse-autoencoder-decomposition. This is a direct mechanistic-understanding input for downstream interpretable-virtual-screening + mechanistic-understanding-of-affinity-prediction + rational-protein-engineering + rational-CRISPR-guide-design + interpretable-cell-type-classification pipelines. The dataset is ABSENT from the id:101-id:109 retention window per regex-dedup and is FIRST promoted to primary feature today.",
